Dear Joost,

I am responding once, and finally, to your messages regarding Jed Boards.

Jed Boards ceased operations years ago after the company became insolvent.
It was a genuine business failure. We delivered product to some customers,
but ultimately we ran out of money, and those we could not refund were left
without recourse when the company was wound down. I personally lost in
excess of one million US dollars in that business. The company no longer
exists, holds no assets, and no refund is possible. This is not going to
change, regardless of how many times or through how many channels the
question is asked.

Your purchase was with Jed Boards as a company. That company failed, and I
regret that you were among those who could not be made whole. But I will
not be paying you US$2,424 personally, now or in the future.

I must now address your conduct. You have contacted my employer about a
private matter that has nothing to do with them, and you have previously
published my home address online. Both are unacceptable. OpusFab is a
separate company with no connection to Jed Boards, and I am asking you
formally to stop contacting my employer, my colleagues, or any organisation
I am associated with, and to stop publishing my personal information. I am
keeping records of all such contact, including this correspondence.

You are entitled to pursue your complaint through the authorities, and they
have had your reports since 2021. That is where this matter belongs. It
does not belong at my workplace or on the internet alongside my home
address.

Please consider this my final response. I will not be engaging further on
this matter.

Jeremy

--000000000000b00788065f3024a6
